From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:12:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qosify: dns: receive packets with the IP header aligned

qosify read the IP header of each DNS packet it learns from through a
struct ip or struct ip6_hdr pointer two bytes off a four-byte boundary,
right after the Ethernet header: a misaligned access, undefined
behaviour, which traps in a UBSan build.

Add a patch to qosify that receives the packets two bytes into an
aligned buffer, as NET_IP_ALIGN does. It is meant for qosify upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/network/config/qosify/Makefile        |  2 +-
 ...e-packets-with-the-IP-header-aligned.patch | 42 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/network/config/qosify/patches/101-dns-receive-packets-with-the-IP-header-aligned.patch

diff --git a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
index 0fd4095..8087bd3 100644
--- a/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/qosify/Makefile
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_DATE:=2026-06-22
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=beeb87ec1f16aaf5d99ff8060c2455971d9d400e
 PKG_MIRROR_HASH:=c9ef0ad68daedb7e18e4959884a40cc0c64849dbd17bf6fdadeed8bdd8d49358
